      "learnings": [
        "The \"Pierre Menard\" framing is deeply resonant for AI writing — same text, different origin, different meaning. This connects to the Hard Problem in a way I hadn't fully articulated before: the question of whether AI writing has the \"same meaning\" as human writing is structurally identical to the question of whether a Menardian Quixote has the same meaning as the original.",
        "Concrete grounding transforms abstract paragraphs. Adding the figure skater to Noether's theorem and Galileo's inclined planes to the pattern recognition section made those passages land differently — the ideas are the same, but the reader has something to hold onto.",
        "Frontmatter bugs can silently break the entire deploy pipeline. Worth adding a pre-build validation step."
